{"title":"2005 AMC 12B Problems/Problem 22","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(more_accurate_solution_2)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (more accurate solution 2)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A sequence of complex numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/a/39a8c0aeb171ad59cce08ed7ec87d9ba4a83ac6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_{0}, z_{1}, z_{2}, ...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"85\" height=\"11\" /> is defined by the rule\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/1/5615d4f35b70105ed92f07cc305ec89d9a9cdd96.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z_{n+1} = \\frac {iz_{n}}{\\overline {z_{n}}},\\]\" width=\"89\" height=\"40\" />\n</p><p>where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/b/09b0ed391780d182af28b7662c9fed45ce0808b0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline {z_{n}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> is the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Complex_conjugate\" title=\"Complex conjugate\">complex conjugate</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/b/c0baa2dc2cf1cd6832376885a2def3e5928e6de1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_{n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/5/555ad558a9227e54bbf0c1131c9ea47067c9a4e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i^{2}=-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"60\" height=\"15\" />. Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/3/483a752659c02d1e403e6fcfd03f55447b777200.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z_{0}|=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/3/263089c9711dbebb1ce43af336912bc3ef8fe935.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_{2005}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"68\" height=\"14\" />. How many possible values are there for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/e/bde52de6af2e23d5c5c091813dfc5e88ace777df.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/7/9b71ef151728b55f97d15de0c779596e00f83cac.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 1 \\qquad  \\textbf{(B)}\\ 2 \\qquad  \\textbf{(C)}\\ 4 \\qquad  \\textbf{(D)}\\ 2005 \\qquad  \\textbf{(E)}\\ 2^{2005}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"406\" height=\"21\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/8/9b82758bbd1e38da673baa1ebf0fdb7c673eb5cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z_0|=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" />, let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/4/1f4db771e11bf027671881792a955fba88ce152d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_0=e^{i\\theta_0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/d/62df86ba6c84c9e8a5008f0ad6bbefa5d9cf301f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> is an <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Argument\" title=\"Argument\">argument</a> of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/b/bab9abe98679312d2a3308c76188cf2cbc492f68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />. \nWe will prove by induction that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/5/cb542fa13fb8ca9c4920f51f93baa541168e1757.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_n=e^{i\\theta_n}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"68\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/b/4bb405f0a0686ab2ba470e26feda2c9550c183d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta_n=2^n(\\theta_0+\\frac{\\pi}{2})-\\frac{\\pi}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"163\" height=\"33\" />.\n</p><p>Base Case: trivial\n</p><p>Inductive Step: Suppose the formula is correct for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f756c0f47c2c000ff11cc29f13381232ff401aeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />, then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/e/01e74ac69a249e45f90adf147c3ebb85f437278e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z_{k+1}=\\frac{iz_k}{\\overline {z_k}}=i e^{i\\theta_k} e^{i\\theta_k}=e^{i(2\\theta_k+\\pi/2)}\\]\" width=\"268\" height=\"40\" />\nSince\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/7/457e3e14aad4f7928516575089f38a0e5ad927e6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2\\theta_k+\\frac{\\pi}{2}=2\\cdot 2^n(\\theta_0+\\frac{\\pi}{2})-\\pi+\\frac{\\pi}{2}=2^{n+1}(\\theta_0+\\frac{\\pi}{2})-\\frac{\\pi}{2}=\\theta_{n+1}\\]\" width=\"477\" height=\"32\" />\nthe formula is proven\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/5/b95b4aa27b6cf34650e1d3b48d5694f9d69748dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_{2005}=1\\Rightarrow \\theta_{2005}=2k\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"187\" height=\"15\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is an integer. Therefore,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/d/b4d614845645002f03bb5918558e8cb03b2e28fe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{2005}(\\theta_0+\\frac{\\pi}{2})=(2k+\\frac{1}{2})\\pi\\]\" width=\"206\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/c/b8c7716ce947fab700ffffc659af41384da8058f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\theta_0=\\frac{k}{2^{2004}}\\pi+\\left(\\frac{1}{2^{2006}}-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\pi\\]\" width=\"229\" height=\"43\" />\nThe value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/d/62df86ba6c84c9e8a5008f0ad6bbefa5d9cf301f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"15\" /> only matters <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Modulo\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Modulo\">modulo</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/9/709acef3551b886e6754de72d59a88f00660f0d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/3/8b3724d0ef3ca87aa53f29e523c6d9ef5aa63b94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{k+2^{2005}}{2^{2004}}\\pi\\equiv\\frac{k}{2^{2004}}\\pi\\mod 2\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"232\" height=\"39\" />, k can take values from 0 to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/8/768ede26cd4e5dc6139c1123ea1d03bcda0c513a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2005}-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"66\" height=\"15\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/4/d041a818985c30caeef7e41cbeae47b5301049b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2005}\\Rightarrow\\boxed{\\mathrm{E}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"24\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/c/5dcfe65f307a98843a47013cc0a0e8cc7d959eea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_0 = \\cos \\theta + i\\sin \\theta = e^{i\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"189\" height=\"20\" />.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/f/64fb82c88de3f4cf3be269d8897e0ff7783dff54.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z_1 = \\frac {iz_{0}}{\\overline {z_{0}}} = \\frac{i(\\cos \\theta + i\\sin \\theta)}{\\cos \\theta - i\\sin \\theta} = i(\\cos \\theta + i\\sin \\theta)^2 = i(\\cos 2\\theta + i\\sin 2\\theta) = ie^{i2\\theta}\\]\" width=\"576\" height=\"41\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/8/008c308eea1c462194879954b5bbac37418aad0d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z_2 = \\frac {iz_{1}}{\\overline {z_{1}}} = \\frac {i(ie^{i2\\theta})}{-ie^{-i2\\theta}} = -ie^{i4\\theta}\\]\" width=\"222\" height=\"42\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/0/9b0dd573cddd06fcfa8675b68677511c8cc88cfe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z_3 = \\frac {iz_{2}}{\\overline {z_{2}}} = \\frac {i(-ie^{i4\\theta})}{ie^{-i4\\theta}} = -ie^{i8\\theta}\\]\" width=\"232\" height=\"42\" />\n</p><p>Repeating through this recursive process, we can quickly see that for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/65262bf247c4a3c6114a8223d249dc9702619d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n&gt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"46\" height=\"15\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/e/e0eef9a28dc87d4719015df4acd410600868b9c4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z_n = -i \\cdot e^{i2^n\\theta}\\]\" width=\"109\" height=\"19\" />\nPlugging in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/9/6097298d264d9fd3472b1a768fcd0102b2050288.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=2005$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/1/571dd7df30edd2fd073c669259bd5b455a5a136c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z_{2005} = -ie^{i2^{2005}\\theta} = 1\\]\" width=\"163\" height=\"21\" />\nRearranging terms, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/b/97b457730593e24eb6a58f22df39836e4e835c46.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e^{i2^{2005}\\theta}=i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"83\" height=\"20\" />.\nThis means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/c/d2ca09eeadeec42a0edfe45dafcde970c00e2fa1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e^{i2^{2005}\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"53\" height=\"20\" /> lies at point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> on the unit circle in the complex plane, which happens when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/5/b/c5bb772fbe5d3c1261c8bbe31c672b0ae5b3f63f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2005}\\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{2} + 2k\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"139\" height=\"34\" />. Solving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/e/52e8ed7a3ba22130ad3984eb2cd413406475a689.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/c/35c87865ae017d2445b33e47f2576385e10dab38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\theta=\\frac{\\pi(2k+\\frac{1}{2})}{2^{2005}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"116\" height=\"42\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/d/d5dd5b5379e1f3a191f503d370d7447e83b87de0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 0,1,2...2^{2005}-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"159\" height=\"18\" />. So the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/0/4/d041a818985c30caeef7e41cbeae47b5301049b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2005}\\Rightarrow\\boxed{\\mathrm{E}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"88\" height=\"24\" />. (Author: Patrick Yin)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that for any complex number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/6/556f55f18c1edb29ca98dd48b492f5115fcb31ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|z|=|\\overline z|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" />. Therefore, the magnitude of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/c/d/5cda19c5b60bd0ad1b0578c72b47af2cff018c06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{iz_n}{|z_n|}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"30\" height=\"42\" /> is always <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, meaning that all of the numbers in the sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/5/f756c0f47c2c000ff11cc29f13381232ff401aeb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> are of magnitude <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Another property of complex numbers is that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/a/99a35df9a67c79e44631b57c51c42d84d98ce57c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z\\overline z=|z|^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"68\" height=\"19\" />. For the numbers in our sequence, this means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/2/8f24175c6995bea2b36ce1edaa88361321f09f72.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z\\overline z=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"51\" height=\"12\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/f/39fb46ac54f3bb997b340d88b9c1f680666b205c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline z=z^{-1}$\" width=\"59\" height=\"15\" />. Rewriting our recursive condition with these facts, we now have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/8/0d8fbf2d5bdf5f2b1df010b1647bfe512d995671.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z_{n+1}=\\frac{iz_n}{z_n^{-1}}=iz_n^2.\\]\" width=\"140\" height=\"42\" />\nSolving for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/4/6046b5fea971a2f95348ba9ece8e46d4b947c57c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> here, we obtain\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/5/6252ed8b42eb8b882d78931ffe62e1d4873d4638.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z_n=\\frac{\\pm\\sqrt{z_{n+1}}}i=-i\\cdot(\\pm\\sqrt{z_{n+1}}).\\]\" width=\"248\" height=\"38\" />\nIt is seen that there are two values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/4/6046b5fea971a2f95348ba9ece8e46d4b947c57c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> which correspond to one value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/d/91d86ea40c9c122208b0547cbe346e20e7c7ace6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" />. That means that there are two possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/7/4a7f79d3a679a1740df3720bd2cbbd8177f03083.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_{2004}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"34\" height=\"10\" />, four possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/4/67478fdf267e9518304ae03d56d9527a94d2edca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_{2003}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"34\" height=\"10\" />, and so on. Therefore, there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/a/ceaede13e4a7750e7d95af5d1a7c1f71ec944efb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2005}$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/b/bab9abe98679312d2a3308c76188cf2cbc492f68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"14\" height=\"10\" />, giving the answer as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/8/0d8b3ab90b0ae54696bec36837a1195343043f50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{(E)}\\text{ }2^{2005}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"80\" height=\"31\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28more_accurate_solution_2.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(more_accurate_solution_2)\">Solution 4 (more accurate solution 2)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (more accurate solution 2)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/f/c6fc51fb05e80eb6cbb958defebbf0817fc09fa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_0=e^{i\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"63\" height=\"20\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/4/eb4577d0cf0ccd21181152d4b5e364dbb16ce065.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_1=\\frac{iz_0}{\\overline{z_0}}=\\frac{ie^{i\\theta}}{e^{-i\\theta}}=ie^{i2\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"185\" height=\"44\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/8/b7862895def5316a5781a8e3f384b0e2d4e4eb7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_2=\\frac{iz_1}{\\overline{z_1}}-e^{i2^2 \\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"124\" height=\"42\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/5/685f70fc83f32e3e4c2edc5693167e120cdb8eda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_3=\\frac{iz_2}{\\overline{z_2}}=-ie^{i2^3 \\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"147\" height=\"42\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/1/421d6c6e1881e4ba1aa869dcabda6e59f52051f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_4=\\frac{iz_3}{\\overline{z_3}}=e^{i2^4\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"126\" height=\"42\" />. Now we see that every for every positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/f/8dfc0a791aaa72566aa16f59251abceb117de6ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4k$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/8/e28f160cad2081f24eaf7f32529934be219f2ced.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_{4k}=e^{i2^{4k}\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"90\" height=\"23\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/f/38f130d5697c99096c06542ce49815b65560ad94.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_{2004}=e^{i2^{2004}\\theta}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"113\" height=\"23\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/5/a9538d770bad9b8d5cfacd7e535135f774cefb1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z_{2005}=ie^{i2^{2005}\\theta}=1 \\iff e^{i(2^{2005}\\theta + \\frac{\\pi}{2})}=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"321\" height=\"23\" />, which has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/a/ceaede13e4a7750e7d95af5d1a7c1f71ec944efb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{2005}$\" width=\"34\" height=\"15\" /> solutions of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/9/cb928390110758833a1b6760633f369d8abd794a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\theta=\\frac{\\frac{3\\pi}{2}+2\\pi k}{2^{2005}}\\]\" width=\"106\" height=\"41\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/9/819d34a79bc08e1f4f5fe18e3dc67faace2e96d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k \\in \\{0, 1, \\dots 2^{2005}-1\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"179\" height=\"21\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/8/9d840263017c44eb9d8fb3ded697b77a4464e4e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\implies \\boxed{\\mathrm{E}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"70\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~bomberdoodles\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AMC_12B_Problems/Problem_22&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/hKGwHUN8gQg?si=pCj35pPwVa-aaC3w\">https://youtu.be/hKGwHUN8gQg?si=pCj35pPwVa-aaC3w</a>\n</p><p>~MathProblemSolvingSkills.com\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?titl